From: Chukun Pan <amadeus@jmu.edu.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: detect W1701K mixed FEM from band 1

The W1701K uses an internal FEM on band 0 and external FEMs on
bands 1 and 2. Probing only the first A-die classifies the board
as internal FEM, so validation rejects its factory EEPROM.

Limit the band 1 probe to the W1701K. Some tri-band boards with
internal FEMs on all bands depend on the band 0 probe.

Link: https://lkml.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/2511.1/01728.html
Link: https://lists.infradead.org/pipermail/linux-mediatek/2025-December/102338.html
---
--- a/mt7996/init.c
+++ b/mt7996/init.c
@@ -1256,7 +1256,8 @@ static int mt7996_variant_fem_init(struc
 		adie_idx = (val & MT_PAD_GPIO_ADIE_SINGLE) ? 0 : 1;
 		adie_comb = u32_get_bits(val, MT_PAD_GPIO_ADIE_COMB_7992);
 	} else {
-		adie_idx = 0;
+		adie_idx = is_mt7996(&dev->mt76) &&
+			of_machine_is_compatible("gemtek,w1701k-ubi") ? 1 : 0;
 		adie_comb = u32_get_bits(val, MT_PAD_GPIO_ADIE_COMB);
 	}
 
